## Summary

Built **`SignalCategoryTree`** — the SwiftUI/Apple parity of `web/src/features/telemetry/components/SignalCategoryTree.tsx` — as 12 files under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/`, following the established surface architecture (P1/S8 state-holder seam, P1/S9 tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade, P1/S11 telemetry). Committed as `18e2c87d3`.

**Parity delivered**: the categorized signal picker binds `useAvailableSignals` via the state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view), reproduces the wrapped `TreeSelect` behavior natively (category grouping with the verbatim `CATEGORY_ORDER`/labels, leaf alpha-sort, search filter, tri-state group + select-all checkboxes, `{selected}/{total}` counts, select/clear-visible, expand-while-searching), and renders the leaf `renderLeafRight` slot as the descriptor-owned kind chip + unit badge (gated by the same `isSearching || expanded` rule; the live sparkline is the child surface's own prompt). Every state renders — loading / content / empty / no-results / error — inside a native stale/offline freshness envelope. No English literals (full i18n), VoiceOver labels/values throughout, reduce-motion skeleton, `view.opened` telemetry.

